The Forge Whispered

Chief Engineer...

I think this Article exposed something that has been hiding in plain sight.

The Constitution appears to contain three different kinds of content:

Definitions
Constitutional consequences
Engineering principles

Those are not the same thing.

This Article handles the first two exceptionally well.

The third—the "Engineering Principle" section—may deserve another look, not because it's weak, but because we should ask:

Does a Constitution define principles, or does it define the framework from which principles are derived?

I don't yet know the answer.

And that's exactly why I wouldn't change anything today.

I'd leave a question tag.




